Sample Bicep Deployment Commands:

Step One: Provision Resources
1 Create full set of AI Agent resources with new dependent resources (Storage, CosmosDB, Search account)
az deployment group create --name ExampleDeployment --resource-group {ResourceGroup Name} --template-file {template path to step1-provision-resources.bicep} --parameters newOrExisting=new foundryAccountName={new foundry account name}

2 Create full set of AI Agent resources with existing dependent resources (Storage, CosmosDB, Search account)

az deployment group create --name ExampleDeployment --resource-group {ResourceGroup Name} --template-file {template path to step1-provision-resources.bicep} --parameters newOrExisting=existing cosmosDBAccountName={BYO CosmosDB account name} storageAccountName={BYO storage account name} aiSearchName={BYO search account name} foundryAccountName={new foundry account name}

Step Two: Grant Role Assignments
az deployment group create --name ExampleDeployment --resource-group {ResourceGroup Name} --template-file {template path to step2-grant-role-assignments.bicep} --parameters storageAccountName={BYO storage account name} searchAccountName={BYO search account name} cosmosdbName={BYO CosmosDB account name} accountName={foundry account name} projectName={foundry project name}

Step Three: Create Capability Host
az deployment group create --name ExampleDeployment --resource-group {ResourceGroup Name} --template-file {template path to step3-create-capability-host.bicep} --parameters storageConnectionName={BYO storage account name} searchConnectionName={BYO search account name} cosmosdbConnectionName={BYO CosmosDB account name} accountName={foundry account name} projectName={foundry project name}

*Why have to do three steps
Due to the role assignment delay and the limitation that Bicep template cannot wait and retry https://github.com/Azure/bicep/issues/1013
We have to break the full setup into three bicep file
Bicep team will have a fix soon. Please refer to discussion in https://github.com/Azure/bicep/issues/1013